## 1. Parties, material and scope

“Licensor” means Santa’s AI Lab Inc. “You” means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this license. If acting for an entity, you must have authority to bind it.

“Covered Material” means only files or other material the Licensor expressly identifies as governed by this license in an accompanying release manifest or file notice, including any identified CAD, PCB design, fabrication files, firmware, software, build scripts and documentation. “Modified Material” means your modifications or adaptations of Covered Material. Identifying a file does not grant rights in third-party content that the Licensor cannot license.

Your “Group” includes you and entities controlling, controlled by, or under common control with you. Control means ownership of more than half the voting interests or the practical power to direct management. Employees and contractors acting solely for a Group do not receive additional sales allowances for that work.

Covered Material excludes third-party material identified under separate terms, trademarks and branding except for Section 5, customer data, credentials, and access to hosted services. No rights in excluded material are implied.

