You may keep modifications private. This license does not require publication of your source or assignment of your modifications. If you distribute, Section 4 applies. Each recipient receives permission for Covered Material directly from the Licensor on these terms; you may not sublicense or waive the Licensor’s sales condition. You may separately license your own original additions if doing so does not purport to remove these terms from Covered Material.

The permission lasts for the applicable rights’ duration unless terminated under Section 8. New license versions do not change rights already granted for a release under this version. Rights under an independently obtained license remain governed by that license.

## 3. Commercial hardware sales allowance

### 3.1 Covered Units

A “Covered Unit” is a physical product incorporating Covered Material, implementing a hardware design included in Covered Material, or incorporating Modified Material, in one of these forms: (a) a complete or substantially complete electronic device; (b) an electronics kit intended to produce one such device; or (c) a main-board printed circuit board assembly intended to form the functional core of one such device. An unpopulated main board sold with the parts intended to complete it is a kit.

One kit intended to build multiple devices counts as that number of units. Combining a main-board assembly and its kit or enclosure into one device does not multiply the count for the same Group. Splitting a complete device or kit into coordinated shipments or transactions does not avoid counting it. Cases, buttons, passive accessories, bare boards supplied without a coordinated kit, and ordinary replacement parts are not Covered Units on their own.

A general-purpose computer is not a Covered Unit solely because it runs the software. A factual reference to Walkie One, a quotation from its documentation, or interoperability with Walkie One does not by itself make an independently designed product a Covered Unit.

### 3.2 What counts as a sale

Your Group may sell up to **100 Covered Units in total** under this license. Count worldwide sales across all Covered Material releases and all product names, modifications, channels and controlled affiliates. The allowance is cumulative, not annual.

A sale is a transfer for money or other commercial consideration, including a paid bundle or hardware supplied in exchange for a subscription commitment. Reserve a unit against the allowance when you accept a binding order, preorder or paid crowdfunding commitment for that unit, or transfer it if earlier. A cancelled order with a full refund before delivery releases its reserved count. A return after delivery does not erase the unit’s count; resale of that same unit does not add a second count. A no-charge, one-for-one repair or warranty replacement that replaces a withdrawn unit does not consume another allowance.

Personal builds, genuinely free gifts, research and internal use without sale do not count. Software downloads and distributions alone are not Covered Units. Pure software sales, hosting without hardware supply, and rental without sale are outside this sales allowance. These exclusions do not grant hosted-service, trademark or third-party rights.

Units made for your Group by a contractor count toward your Group when sold by or for it. A contractor working solely to your documented order may rely on your remaining allowance for that work and must not distribute those units independently. Ordinary resale of lawfully supplied, authorized units does not consume a new allowance and does not create an allowance for newly manufactured units. Applicable exhaustion and first-sale rights are preserved.

A renamed product, new release, affiliate, intermediary or artificial division of one business does not reset its count. On a transfer of the relevant business to a successor, its used allowance follows that business; a transaction does not create a fresh allowance for its continuing sales. Keep reasonable aggregate records sufficient to establish the number of units and authorized resales. This license does not require telemetry, customer-level reporting, access to your systems or routine audits.

### 3.3 Permission beyond 100

Before accepting a sale that would bring your Group above 100 Covered Units, obtain a **separate written commercial license signed by an authorized representative of the Licensor**. A request, silence, quotation, verbal discussion, or payment for an ordinary product is not permission. Requests may be sent to contact@walkieone.com.

Until that agreement is effective, this license grants no rights to make the excess sales. The Licensor may approve or decline a request and may propose separate terms. There is no automatic fee, royalty schedule or right to approval. Reaching 100 lawful sales does not revoke permission for personal use, research, internal use, modifications or distribution of files permitted elsewhere in this license. It creates no retroactive payment obligation for earlier compliant sales. Manufacturing inventory does not itself reserve permission to sell beyond the allowance.

