When distributing Covered Material or Modified Material, include this license and relevant copyright, patent, attribution and third-party notices. Identify that you made modifications, where applicable, without suggesting they came from the Licensor. Preserve notices for the material you use; unrelated notices need not be reproduced.

For a distributed Covered Unit, provide these notices in accompanying documentation, on an accessible device information screen, or through a durable link printed in its accompanying documentation. Identify yourself as the maker or seller and use a factual attribution such as “Based on the Walkie One design.” No logo or exterior imprint is required.

You must not represent that you grant unrestricted rights to the original Covered Material or that downstream manufacturers are exempt from Section 3. Recipients may rely on this license for their own permitted uses. Third-party components remain under their own terms; this license does not add restrictions to rights those terms grant. If combining materials would create incompatible obligations, do not distribute the combination without resolving them.

